Nevertheless, vacuum-to-vacuum diagrams do shift the vacuum energy. In $\lambda\phi^4$ theory, join the four legs of one quartic vertex into two short loops. Each coincident propagator supplies $1/\delta^2$, so $\delta\rho_{\mathrm{vac}}
\sim
c_{\mathrm{vac}}\frac{\lambda}{\delta^4}.$ More complicated vacuum diagrams carry different coupling factors and coefficients, but dimensional analysis typically leaves the same quartic cutoff sensitivity for an energy density.

